  "description": "The extremes of the declared widths. One record holds the smallest values the spans can carry - ACCT-ID 00000000000 and every monetary span at positive zero - and one holds the largest, ACCT-ID 99999999999 with 99999999999I, which is nine in the low-order digit position with a positive overpunch and therefore the maximum a twelve-character S9(10)V99 span represents. A third record sits between them. DISPLAY concatenates its operands at their declared widths, so no value here may be shortened, padded differently or re-aligned.",
